Churro: Ctrl+Alt+Del must not hard-reset the machine.

We enable the VT console (fbcon, on-screen boot log), which also attaches the kernel's VT
keyboard handler; its Ctrl+Alt+Del calls kernel_restart() at once (no Android shutdown, no
filesystem sync). Googlebook kernels have no VT, so the keys never did this there. With C_A_D off
the kernel only sends SIGINT to init, which ignores it.

--- a/kernel/reboot.c
+++ b/kernel/reboot.c
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
  * this indicates whether you can reboot with ctrl-alt-del: the default is yes
  */
 
-static int C_A_D = 1;
+static int C_A_D = 0;
 struct pid *cad_pid;
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(cad_pid);
 
